    {
      "file": "scenes/scene-2.js",
      "narration": "You don't need a special font, just one that renders the same everywhere. Use one family in two weights, or pair a serif headline with a plain sans-serif body.",
      "storyboard": "Paper stage. On 'renders the same everywhere' four name tags slide in on a row: Calibri, Arial, Segoe UI, Georgia, each set in its own face, with small check marks. On 'one family in two weights' the row clears and a single word appears in Bold over Regular, left half of frame. On 'serif headline' a Georgia headline drops into the right half, and on 'sans-serif body' an Arial body line settles beneath it, a teal bracket pairing them. Caption at bottom: 'Contrast, don't compete.'",
      "minDuration": 11,
      "slide": {
        "title": "Use reliable fonts and pair them carefully",
