      "file": "scenes/scene-3.js",
      "narration": "Headlines at 36 to 44 point, body text 24 point or larger, chart labels 18 point minimum, and bigger still for video. If it won't fit at 24, cut words.",
      "storyboard": "Night stage, a vertical type-scale ruler on the left. On 'Headlines' a block grows to the 36–44pt mark in paper white, on 'body text' a 24pt marker locks in signal yellow, on 'chart labels' an 18pt floor line appears in teal, on 'bigger still for video' every block scales up together. On 'cut words' a crowded paragraph tries to squeeze in at 24pt, overflows in coral, and words strike out until it fits. The bullet list is rebuilt as this animated scale.",
      "minDuration": 12,
      "slide": {
        "title": "Set body text at 24pt or larger",
        "text": "Headlines 36 to 44pt. Body text 24pt or larger. Chart labels 18pt minimum. Bigger still for video",
        "notes": "If text won't fit at twenty-four point, the slide has too much on it. Cut words, split the slide, or move the detail into your speaker notes.",
